A vendored snapshot of Christoph Dalitz's standalone C++ interface to Daniel
Müllner's fastcluster, copied verbatim (fastcluster.h, fastcluster.cpp,
fastcluster_dm.cpp, fastcluster_R_dm.cpp) plus upstream's LICENSE. Do not edit
these by hand -- re-vendor and update this file.

Why vendored: speaker diarization ends in a clustering step, grouping the
embedding of every window of speech by whose voice it is. That is agglomerative
hierarchical clustering, which is a solved problem with a subtle
implementation: the naive form is O(n^3) and this recording is thousands of
windows. Müllner's is the fastest published implementation and the one behind
scipy's linkage, so writing our own would be slower, longer and less tested.

What we use, in src/diarize/cluster.cpp:
  hclust_fast    average-linkage over a condensed cosine-distance matrix
  cutree_k       cut at a known speaker count
  cutree_cdist   cut at a distance, for when the count is not known

fastcluster_dm.cpp and fastcluster_R_dm.cpp are #included by fastcluster.cpp
rather than compiled separately; that is upstream's arrangement, not ours.

